description: Import from the concrete module; do not add barrel index re-exports
alwaysApply: true
---

# No barrel exports

A barrel is `index.ts` that `export *` (or re-exports a folder) so callers import from the folder instead of the file. That hides the source, weakens tree-shaking, and couples consumers to a grab-bag. Import the module that defines the symbol.

Do not add `src/index.ts` that re-exports the package. A public API, if we ever need one, lists named exports explicitly — never `export *`.

```typescript
// ❌
export * from './grid-strategy';
import { just } from 'true-myth';
import { formatDate } from './date/index';

// ✅
import { just } from 'true-myth/maybe';
import { createWallClock } from '@enormora/wall-clock/wall-clock';
import { onTick } from './grid-strategy';
```

ESLint `no-barrel-files/no-barrel-files` and `prefer-source-imports` are **error**.
